From: meo <chenevard.romeo@gmail.com>
Date: 2026-06-17
Subject: [PATCH] logind: fix session lock monitor not bound on fresh startup

LogindService::setSessionLockIntegrationEnabled() returns early when the
new value matches the cached one. m_sessionLockIntegrationEnabled defaults
to `true`, so on fresh app startup with `lockscreen.enabled = true` the
initial call setSessionLockIntegrationEnabled(true) is true→true and skips
ensureSessionLockMonitor() — the dbus session proxy is never constructed
and the Lock/Unlock signals are never subscribed.

Result: `loginctl lock-session` (or any equivalent) does not trigger
noctalia's lockscreen on fresh startup. Workaround would be toggling the
config option after startup to force a false→true transition.

Cleanest fix is to flip the default to `false` so the first call with
`true` always performs the transition. ensureSessionLockMonitor() has its
own internal m_sessionProxy null-guard so repeated invocations are safe.

Filed upstream at: <to-be-added when issue is posted>

--- a/src/dbus/logind/logind_service.h
+++ b/src/dbus/logind/logind_service.h
@@ -30,7 +30,7 @@ private:
   SystemBus& m_bus;
   std::unique_ptr<sdbus::IProxy> m_managerProxy;
   std::unique_ptr<sdbus::IProxy> m_sessionProxy;
-  bool m_sessionLockIntegrationEnabled = true;
+  bool m_sessionLockIntegrationEnabled = false;
   PrepareForSleepCallback m_prepareForSleepCallback;
   SessionLockCallback m_lockCallback;
   SessionLockCallback m_unlockCallback;
